Needs codex-vm -board-mmio, which the default harness does not pass. The STM32L4 driver touches the Cortex-M System Control Block at 0xE000ED00, above the RAM ceiling; since 2026-07-13 the guest page tables map the device gigabyte and codex-vm can back that window with -board-mmio, and this test then passes (13). Run it from build/boards-test.ps1, which is where the nine board batteries live.
